From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 02:43:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 001/190] Add Sega CD (Mega CD) sub-CPU machine target

EmuTOS runs on the Sega CD's sub 68000, whose address 0 is PRG-RAM, so
the ST low-memory ABI holds byte-authentic. The OS image links at
0x080000 (Word RAM). No Atari hardware; a servant firmware on the
Genesis-side main 68000 converts the ST-low planar screen to VDP tiles
and will deliver input. Machine layer modeled on the Apple Lisa port:

- bios/segacd.c/h/segacd2.S: screen hooks (ST-low, stock top-of-RAM
  buffer), gate-array timer as the 200 Hz system tick (INT3), VBL from
  the main CPU (INT2), keyboard/clock stubs
- config: CONF_ATARI_HARDWARE 0, CONF_STRAM_SIZE 384K, no floppy
- Makefile: 'segacd' target -> emutos-segacd.img (make clean first,
  as between any two targets)
